Code caches stay in use after a DEP change (FEX 3bec2ac, on top of 0026)

NFSU2 ran 64 blocks of the 32-bit ntdll in FEX's NoJIT interpreter in
every run, although each round compiled them into the AOT image. The
game's image has no NX_COMPAT, so the 32-bit ntdll's loader turns DEP off
for the process (NtSetInformationProcess(ProcessExecuteFlags)), Wine's
wow64 calls BTCpuNotifyProcessExecuteFlagsChange, and the invalidation
tracker drops every block in the guest window:

  [code-inval] DEP setting changed: 0x0-0x100000000 dropped 7806 blocks

That includes every block the code caches registered, and nothing
registered them again, so whatever ran after that came from the JIT, or
under NoJIT from the interpreter.

The change drops compiled code because a block compiled with DEP on can
hold a NoExec stub for an address that is executable now. A code cache's
blocks were compiled offline from the image's code sections, which are
executable whatever the DEP setting, so they are still right:

- InvalidationTracker::HandleProcessExecuteFlagsChange says whether it
  dropped anything (the setting really changed);
- BTCpuNotifyProcessExecuteFlagsChange then has ImageTracker register
  the blocks of every loaded code cache again (ReenableLoadedCaches,
  "[aot-cache] registering the loaded code caches again after a DEP
  change dropped their blocks"); EnableLoadedSection does not apply a
  cache page's relocations twice (LoadedPages);
- an unmapped image's cache is never registered again (its Image
  pointer pointed into MappedImages and is cleared on unmap).

diff --git a/Source/Windows/Common/ImageTracker.cpp b/Source/Windows/Common/ImageTracker.cpp
index eb25e23..1ddfbb4 100644
--- a/Source/Windows/Common/ImageTracker.cpp
+++ b/Source/Windows/Common/ImageTracker.cpp
@@ -223,6 +223,17 @@ void ImageTracker::HandleImageUnmap(uint64_t Address, uint64_t Size) {
   CTX.RemoveForceTSOInformation(Address, Size);
 
   std::unique_lock Lk {ImagesLock};
+#ifdef FEX_IOS_HOST
+  {
+    // The cache's Image points into MappedImages; an unmapped image's cache is never enabled again.
+    std::scoped_lock CachesLk {LoadedCachesLock};
+    for (auto& Loaded : LoadedCaches) {
+      if (auto It = MappedImages.find(Address); It != MappedImages.end() && Loaded.Image == &It->second) {
+        Loaded.Image = nullptr;
+      }
+    }
+  }
+#endif
   MappedImages.erase(Address);
 }
 
@@ -330,7 +341,7 @@ void ImageTracker::LoadImageCache(const MappedImageInfo& Image, std::string_view
 void ImageTracker::EnableLoadedCaches(FEXCore::Core::InternalThreadState* Thread) {
   std::scoped_lock Lk {LoadedCachesLock};
   for (auto& Loaded : LoadedCaches) {
-    if (Loaded.Enabled) {
+    if (Loaded.Enabled || !Loaded.Image) {
       continue;
     }
     Loaded.Enabled = true;
@@ -339,6 +350,17 @@ void ImageTracker::EnableLoadedCaches(FEXCore::Core::InternalThreadState* Thread
     LogMan::Msg::EFmt("[aot-cache] enabled {} at guest {:#x}", Loaded.Image->Info.Filename, Loaded.GuestBegin);
   }
 }
+
+void ImageTracker::ReenableLoadedCaches(FEXCore::Core::InternalThreadState* Thread) {
+  {
+    std::scoped_lock Lk {LoadedCachesLock};
+    for (auto& Loaded : LoadedCaches) {
+      Loaded.Enabled = false;
+    }
+  }
+  LogMan::Msg::EFmt("[aot-cache] registering the loaded code caches again after a DEP change dropped their blocks");
+  EnableLoadedCaches(Thread);
+}
 #endif
 
